{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RCA (rebar-debug Phase 1 complete — four independent lenses: code-tracer, historical, empirical, external/OSS; all converged).\n\nCONFIRMED ROOT CAUSE (regression, caused_by 73b8-2d79-3046-44ce, introducing commit 6a5c88027c5 / change 2100): the per-test budget was lowered 300s -> 20s (pyproject.toml ini + --timeout=20 on both shared-tier workflow lanes) while ~14 legitimate tests cost 18.7-29.9s on the covered ubuntu legs (coverage is a measured ~2x multiplier: 2.75->5.48s, 2.69->5.08s, 1.65->3.85s locally; the remainder is CI hardware + full-suite contention — the parent baseline's own --durations block proves the absolute costs). With timeout_method=thread, expiry executes os._exit(1) (pytest_timeout.py:542), killing the whole xdist worker: hence \"node down: Not properly terminated\", zero \"Failed: Timeout\" lines (thread method bypasses pytest reporting — upstream-documented \"test runs are not completed\"), and the consequential coverage failure (dead workers never flush data; pytest-xdist #466).\n\nWHY THE FIRST FIX (change 2115) FAILED ITS OWN GATE — two independent, proven mechanisms:\n1. Workflow-text provenance: the Gerrit Verified Gate is a workflow_dispatch on main; GitHub resolves ./-referenced reusable workflows at the CALLER'S commit (documented guarantee), so the run executes _build-and-test.yml from trusted main — run 32587991195's referenced_workflows shows _build-and-test.yml@6a5c88027c5, not the patchset sha. A patchset that fixes workflow text can never pass its own gate; it must be merged externally (as it was).\n2. Precedence: pytest-timeout resolves marker > CLI > env > ini (pytest_timeout.py:352-409; verified at runtime, exact CI signature reproduced). 2115's ini bump was inert against main's CLI --timeout=20 regardless. (A conftest-applied marker IS patchset-effective — verified — the viable channel if this recurs.)\n\nHOUR-BURN MECHANISM (verified locally): loadgroup/loadscope requeues the dead node's whole pending workload INCLUDING the crashing item (loadscope.py:166-205), so every respawned worker re-runs it and dies again, up to the default restart cap of numprocesses*4 (dsession.py:555-568) — one 20s-timeout test cost 183s at -n 2 locally; at integration scale this burns toward the 60-min job ceiling. Upstream: pytest-xdist #1094 (our exact scenario), #1189 (registered_collections KeyError cascade; fixes unmerged), #658. worksteal does not re-dispatch the crash item (verified: 1 failed vs 9 failed on the identical scenario). A literal indefinite controller hang was NOT reproduced locally on macOS; the re-dispatch amplification is the confirmed mechanism.\n\nWHY \"CLEAN AT 20s\" ESCAPED: 73b8's measurement was a local unit-tier run (no coverage, no integration/scripts tiers, faster cores); its own plan-review flagged the overgeneralization. Operator ruling was \"20s WITH explicit override for slow tests\", not 20s-everywhere-unmarked.\n\nFIX: change 2115 (a42a9d8d494, \"Lift the hang budget above legitimate cost\") restores timeout=300 in ini + both lanes; merged to main by the operator (the only provenance-valid path). Replication = green Verified runs on post-merge main; in flight at time of writing.\n\nRESIDUAL RISK (follow-up pending operator-conditional approval): method=thread + --dist loadgroup remains the documented cascade combination if any test hangs again; candidate mitigation --max-worker-restart=0 on the loadgroup lane, gated on evidence that maintained OSS projects adopt it (research in flight). External research also flags: signal method is viable on our POSIX runners but cannot interrupt non-GIL-releasing C blocks and silently downgrades off-main-thread."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787423421991161001,"uuid":"dec69a47-2c87-4745-be6f-47842dc75aff"}